    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Bidding (Otea)**: Dealer's opponents place one card face-up. This signifies their desire for that suit to be trumps. 2. **Trump Flip**: Dealer turns up the top card of the stock. This suit becomes trump. If an opponent bid that suit, they swap their bid card for the trump card. 3. **The Play**: Lead any card. Others play any card (no follow-suit requirement). 4. **Winning**: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest card of the led suit wins. 5. **Drawing**: Winner 'eats' the trick, draws a new card from the stock first, then others draw. Lead next. 6. **Endings**: Play continues until stock and hands are empty.",
    Player: "1. **Bidding (Otea)**: Dealer's opponents place one card face-up. This signifies their desire for that suit to be trumps. 2. **Trump Flip**: Dealer turns up the top card of the stock. This suit becomes trump. If an opponent bid that suit, they swap their bid card for the trump card. 3. **The Play**: Lead any card. Others play any card (no follow-suit requirement). 4. **Winning**: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest card of the led suit wins. 5. **Drawing**: Winner 'eats' the trick, draws a new card from the stock first, then others draw. Lead next. 6. **Endings**: Play continues until stock and hands are empty.",
    objective: 'Capture tricks containing high-value cards to surpass 60 points (out of 120 total).',
    gameplay: "1. **Bidding (Otea)**: Dealer's opponents place one card face-up. This signifies their desire for that suit to be trumps. 2. **Trump Flip**: Dealer turns up the top card of the stock. This suit becomes trump. If an opponent bid that suit, they swap their bid card for the trump card. 3. **The Play**: Lead any card. Others play any card (no follow-suit requirement). 4. **Winning**: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest card of the led suit wins. 5. **Drawing**: Winner 'eats' the trick, draws a new card from the stock first, then others draw. Lead next. 6. **Endings**: Play continues until stock and hands are empty.",
    keyRules: [
      'Card Values: Ace=11, 7=10, King=4, Jack=3, Queen=2. Total in deck = 120.',
      'Ndoa (Marriage): When a 7 is captured by an Ace of the same suit.',
      'Mrithi (Target): To avoid a double-loss, you must reach a minimum point threshold (10 for individuals, 20 for 4-player teams, 30 for 6-player teams).',
      'No follow-suit requirement: You can play any card at any time.',
